>What if monsters could learn spells from spellbooks they found in the
>dungeon?  Clearly this would depend on the level of the monster and
>it's proficiency in that particular school of magic.

Yikes - wouldn't it be unbalancing (at least for some spells) ?

>Reason I ask is that my pet Arch-Lich keeps picking up spell books,
>and I thought it would be cool if he could learn stuff.

Pet monsters seem to "forget" some of their cool abilities: dragons
don't vomit and casters won't cast offensive spells, perhaps because
of the game balance.

As for arch-liches, I'm not sure if they can learn _new_ spells, assuming
that they have died too long ago, and while their bodies and mana 
are intact, their mind has decayed too much for the arch-lich to learn
anything new. So, liches hang on to their old ways of wandering around
the dungeons. "Can't teach an old dog any new tricks."

